Lunar Sample Compendium and Astromaterials 3D — NASA ARES (@mp-nasa: 0, is #reference, #part-of @mp-sources) { r_0G134FXVGFCP2KPGXK4Q2W93B3
Charles Meyer, compiler, NASA Astromaterials Research and Exploration Science. [Lunar Sample Compendium, introduction, sample records, and references](https://curator.jsc.nasa.gov/lunar/lsc/) · [NASA Astromaterials 3D](https://ares.jsc.nasa.gov/astromaterials3d/).

Use selected identified lunar/meteorite specimens and complete original papers for a comparative petrology study. Preserve collection/sample identifiers, sub-sample and preparation identity, imaging conditions, published chemistry, textures, ages, and interpretation. A digital specimen model provides another observation window rather than every required mineral/chemical measurement.

The official compendium and 3D collection entrances were accessible on 29 October 2026; full interactive operation was not tested. Preserve actual NASA, contributor, specimen-record, and third-party notices rather than assuming every linked publication/model has identical terms. Sources and models remain external; no sample/media collection or new renderer is added here.

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology sources — books, laboratories, analytical methods, and research](../Sources.lingua#r_38Q6Z3J7ER2G1B441JXJ14NV5A).
